{
  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan, gating, reviews, and rollback. MRS respects the repository constraints: it excludes the flaky network check from required CI, limits full regression to a staged nightly run, and assigns the irreversible schema review to the downstream reporting lead as required. NBG suggests quarantining the flaky test (adding work) and running full regression on every staging deploy despite CI cost, and puts schema review with the SRE instead of the reporting team, which conflicts with the stated process. Therefore MRS more directly matches the team's constraints and reduces follow‑up effort.",
  "verdict": "MRS"
}
